 ],
 "checker_failure": "an output sample more than atol from its expected value: code_3..code_0, done, sample_dbg, dac_dbg of the top module, or an output of a stand-alone module",
 "semantics": "Verilog-A LRM 2.4 5.10.3.1 cross (event within its time tolerance, 1 ps in the reference), 4.5.8 transition (interrupted and delayed transitions), 5.10.3.3 timer; module instances evaluate at the same event time point; to be recorded on Spectre",
 "conditions": {
  "alt_gold_style_continuous": "comparator and DAC evaluated continuously, as in the v4:342 gold: accepted provided the simulator takes a time point within 0.1*g of each input crossing (the module cases put a PWL corner there; the top decides 4 ns later)",
  "alt_delayed_within_tr": "uses a 0.2*tr transport delay; output-changing events are at least 100 ps apart, so no change arrives while an earlier delayed transition is still pending",
  "margin_arrival_1p2tr": "arrives after the tr deadline but before the 1.25*tr scoring start; accepted under the user-confirmed observation rule (F01 A, 2026-10-28), not a correct model",
  "original_v4_342_gold": "the five released v4:342 gold modules unchanged (same module names and ports); its DAC is vss + vref*code/16, the span reading the user did not choose; generated only inside the repository (it reads benchmark/material/historyref)",
  "sample_en_cleared_at_next_edge": "rejected in reset-recovery-long-tr and zero-plateau-from-above provided the sample-and-hold, at the clock edge that clears sample_en, still reads sample_en high (LRM 4.5.8, as the reference at its sample edge); the reset of an armed conversion comes 2*tr plus a 9.375 ps design margin before the edge in reset-recovery-long-tr (the limit of the reset-recovery rule; p0u17-fix-r4, a separation exactly at it is a tie) and 3 ns before it in zero-plateau-from-above",
  "reset_recovery": "p0-fix-b F03 (decided by the user on 2026-10-29, decision sheet item 5): in top cases a clock edge that rst lets through is at least 2*tr after the latest rising rst crossing, so a controller whose sample_en meets its tr deadline has pulled it low by then; reset-recovery-long-tr (tr = 1 ns) holds three resets 2*tr plus a 9.375 ps design margin before the next clock edge (p0u17-fix-r4)",
  "comparator_cross_latch": "the comparator of the reference before p0-fix-e (cross() latch, initial_step from the level; the comparator code equals that of the old solution/circuit.va, only the comment above it differs); rejected in zero-plateau-vss, zero-plateau-from-below and zero-plateau-from-above provided the simulator fires no cross() event when the internal comparator difference leaves an exact-zero plateau (the archived Spectre arrival rule: an event on arrival at 0, none on departure); the Spectre 21.1 results of probe spectre-P0probe-C109-v1, formally accepted on 2026-10-29 (execution identity spectre-P0probe-C109-v1（结果包 sha256 2c4e79eb7fa60d24…）), show it for the old reference on the same stimuli (codes 15, 15 and 10 then 0); under a sign-change-only rule only zero-plateau-vss rejects it; legacy EVAS 0.8.7 accepts it in all three, masked by its zero handling (template r2.16 section 4 item 4); accepted in the eight earlier cases, whose zero plateaus all leave toward positive values or last to the end of the record",
  "comparator_initial_high": "rejected in modules-initial by its initial value (all semantics); it keeps the cross() latch of the reference before p0-fix-e, so it is also rejected in the three zero-plateau cases under the condition of comparator_cross_latch (in the top the difference is 0 at t = 0, where initial_step high = 1 equals the level rule)",
  "zero_plateau": "p0-fix-e: in zero-plateau-vss (the plateau from t = 0) and zero-plateau-from-below (a plateau entered from below at a reset) the internal comparator difference of the top leaves the exact-zero plateau toward negative values, because the next sample is x = vss; in zero-plateau-from-above it enters the plateau from above at a reset and leaves it toward positive values with x >= DAC(8). The reference and every candidate with a level or continuous comparator decide there by the sign of x - DAC(T), independent of the zero semantics; only comparator_cross_latch and comparator_initial_high depend on them",
  "all": "every expectation assumes cross() events within a few ps of the crossing and that a module reading another module's transition() output at a clock event sees the value from before that event (LRM 4.5.8); the reference itself relies on this between the controller and the sample-and-hold"
 },
